<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<ModMetaData>
	<name>The Dead Man's Switch - Taktikmagier</name>
	<modIconPath IgnoreIfNoMatchingField="True">UI/NaraLogo</modIconPath>
  	<author>AobaKuma ,Bill Doors, KV4EX</author>
	<!--
		1.5 is deliberately not listed. LoadFolders.xml only declares a <v1.6> node, and when a
		LoadFolders.xml exists but has no entry for the running version RimWorld loads nothing at
		all from the mod - not even the root folder. Re-adding 1.5 here requires a <v1.5> node in
		LoadFolders.xml and a 1.5/ folder with its own Assemblies build.
	-->
    <supportedVersions>
		<li>1.6</li>
	</supportedVersions>
	<packageId>Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Taktikmagier</packageId>
    <modDependencies>
        <li>
			<packageId>Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core</packageId>
			<steamWorkshopUrl>https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3121742525</steamWorkshopUrl>
			<displayName>Dead Man Switch</displayName>
		</li>		
		<li>
			<packageId>VanillaExpanded.VPsycastsE</packageId>
			<displayName>Vanilla Psycasts Expanded</displayName>
			<steamWorkshopUrl>https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2842502659</steamWorkshopUrl>
		</li>
	</modDependencies>
	<loadAfter>
		<li>Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core</li>
		<li>brrainz.harmony</li>
		<li>VanillaExpanded.VPsycastsE</li>
		<li>vanillaexpanded.achievements</li>
  	</loadAfter>
	<description>Millennia earlier, as the threat of archotech war machines, pirates and awry bio-organic weapons arise. Nara Industries initiated a project of semi-automated war-machines, which aimed at creating a legion of war-machines with low technology and maintenance requirements to aid humans in all galaxy to the war against all those threats.</description>
</ModMetaData>